ution of the First Philippine Republic, drafted by a revolutionary congress at Barasoain church in Malolos, Bulacan, from…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/malorix"><span class="enc-name">Malorix</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Malorix was a leader of the Frisii in the mid-1st century CE, named by Tacitus with Verritus as ruling the people 'as far as Germans are ruled'.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/malta"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/malta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Malta</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Malta is an island country in the central Mediterranean, south of Sicily, made up of Malta, Gozo and smaller islands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/maltese-language"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maltese-language.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Maltese language</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Maltese is the national language of Malta and an official language of the European Union.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maluku-islands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Maluku Islands</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Maluku Islands, or Moluccas, are an archipelago in eastern Indonesia, historically known as the Spice Islands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/malwa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/malwa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Malwa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Malwa is a region of west-central India, on a plateau north of the Nar